Little is known of Wind's background and early history, and nobody, not even his [[Blood Spiral]] brothers and sisters, know what he hides under his mask. {{Source|TCG:OAL-031|OAL-031}} He was revealed as a member of the [[Blood Spiral]] core group, the [[Blooded Circle]], an elite of master Seekers who command and control the Spirals only under the orders of [[Rassimov]] and [[the Betrayer]], himself. {{source|Zhalia's Mission}} 

He and [[Shauna]] met with [[Rassimov]] in the Black Forest, who sent them to attack [[Dante Vale]] and his team, taking from them the [[Amulet of Will]] and [[Eathon Lambert's journal]] on behalf of [[the Professor]] whom Rassimov was deceiving. During the altercation, Wind overpowered Dante and knocked him into the wall of a house before the {{source|The Secret of Two Generations}} Wind, along with Shauna, later met Rassimov after Dante was tricked into thinking Rassimov had been defeated and sucked into his own trap and into taking the [[Amulet]] of [[Archwarder]]. Within a hall emblazoned with the mark of the [[Blood Spiral]], the three then discussed the coming fall of [[the Professor]] and his [[the Organization|Organization]] to Archwarder and the subsequent rising of the Spiral from the shadows of history. {{source|The Divine Comedy}}

Wind, along with [[Shauna]] and [[Shakrit]], later burst into [[Klaus' laboratory]] in order to retrieve the Amulet of the [[Nullifier]], [[Void]], which the [[Huntik Foundation]] was also after. Wind defeated [[Wilder]] with ease as the Spiral claimed the coveted Amulet. {{source|The Blood Spiral}} In [[Rotterdam]], while Rassimov was branding the mark of the Blood Spiral on [[Den Fears|Den]] and [[Harrison Fears]] and the rest of the orphans, Wind guarded the orphanage. He later fought Dante and [[Caliban|Powerbonded Caliba]] on the [[Erasmus Bridge]] but he and Shauna were incapacitated by Dante's [[Stopglue]] spell. {{source|Den vs Harrison}} 

Wind and Shauna later attempted to recover the [[Ring]] of [[Phoenix]] from [[Phoenix Volcano]], however they were delayed by the anti-magic field of the [[Lodestone]]. {{source|The Dead Magic Island}} After Dante's team destroyed the Lodestone, they launched a surprise attack on Wind and Shauna using their newly restored powers. Wind was taken captive but managed to silently escape before bombarding the team with attacks. After invoking [[Shakrit]], Wind fought and overpowered Dante but was forced to flee with Shauna when [[Sophie Casterwill]] dived into the volcano which erupted. {{source|The Phoenix's Ashes}} 

During the final battle at the [[Spiral Mark]], Wind fought against [[Dante]] while [[Lok]] drove the [[Willblade]] into the Mark. Wind witnessed Rassimov and Dante's deaths and the destruction of the [[Red Comet]]. {{source|The Spiral Mark}}
[[File:S2E52_Wind_fall_2.png|170px|thumb|Wind's demise as his body falls through the air]]
Wind later fought against the combined [[Casterwill family]] and [[Huntik Foundation]] alliance when [[the Betrayer]] revealed himself.  In the confrontation, he defeated [[Lucas Casterwill]] and his team. {{source|Lok and the Betrayer}} He later made numerous attacks on the alliance's [[Scramjets]], destroying one of them. However, Shakrit was defeated by [[Momax]] and [[Montehue]] with the Hammer, [[Mjolnir]], sending Wind falling through the air. {{source|Dante's Return}}

